  "title": "Neuer Standort Im Eth Hauptgebaeude",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Exhibition due to open in the coming year",
      "text": "As of now, the Thomas Mann Archives are housed in the ETH main building. Readers can now enjoy easier access and the professionally equipped infrastructure of the Reading Room Collections and Archives in the ETH Library.\n\nWith this move to the main building, the Thomas Mann Archives have left their temporary location at Hönggerberg, where they had been given a home since 2016, and returned to their origins. When the Archives were established in 1956, they were temporarily housed in the ETH main building before being moved to the nearby Bodmerhaus in 1961.\n\nFollowing the relocation, the permanent exhibition of Thomas Mann’s study and private library remains temporarily closed. On 28 February 2023, a redesigned permanent exhibition and the special exhibition “Thomas Mann. Europe Beware!” will open in the ETH main building."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Any questions?",
      "text": "If you need information about the archives and individual objects from the collection or require support with your research, feel free to send an email to the Thomas Mann Archives:\n\nThe Thomas Mann Archives at ETH Zurich preserve the literary works and personal papers of Thomas Mann. They have made his literary legacy available for researchers and the public since the archives’ foundation in 1956. The holdings are constantly updated."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Always up to date",
      "text": "#KnowHow – The ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal. Room for more – Experience variety and exchange"
    }
  ],
